WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:49.960 --> 00:01:53.800
<b>Landfall in Alabasta</b>

3
00:01:54.510 --> 00:01:58.470
<b>Nanohana
Kingdom of Alabasta</b>

4
00:02:10.610 --> 00:02:12.900
So this is one of Alabasta's cities?

5
00:02:12.900 --> 00:02:14.780
Food!

6
00:02:14.780 --> 00:02:16.660
Listen, guys!

7
00:02:16.660 --> 00:02:19.540
Practice self-control
instead of acting on instinct!

8
00:02:19.540 --> 00:02:21.790
Yes, Nami!

9
00:02:21.790 --> 00:02:25.500
The guy who most needed
to hear that is already gone.

10
00:02:25.500 --> 00:02:28.250
Food place!

11
00:02:28.250 --> 00:02:29.210
Get back here!

12
00:02:29.210 --> 00:02:31.300
Nothing but instinct.

13
00:02:31.300 --> 00:02:32.380
What should we do?

14
00:02:32.380 --> 00:02:34.050
Don't worry.

15
00:02:34.630 --> 00:02:37.850
Find the biggest commotion,
and he'll be there.

16
00:02:37.850 --> 00:02:39.100
Bingo.

17
00:02:39.100 --> 00:02:43.810
Ugh! He needs to be more aware
of that bounty on his head,

18
00:02:43.810 --> 00:02:46.060
especially in a big country like this!

19
00:02:46.060 --> 00:02:48.360
Don't worry about him.
Let's just eat first.

20
00:02:48.360 --> 00:02:51.480
We'll strategize more after that.

21
00:02:52.530 --> 00:02:53.740
They're all the same...

22
00:02:56.110 --> 00:02:57.120
What's wrong?

23
00:02:58.530 --> 00:03:00.620
Mr. 3's ship!

24
00:03:02.250 --> 00:03:04.500
That creep didn't kick
the bucket after all?!

25
00:03:04.500 --> 00:03:05.870
No mistaking it!

26
00:03:05.870 --> 00:03:09.250
His ship runs on the power
of his Wax-Wax Fruit!

27
00:03:09.250 --> 00:03:10.750
The bastard's here?

28
00:03:10.750 --> 00:03:12.130
This is bad.

29
00:03:12.760 --> 00:03:21.260
Food pla-a-a-a-a-ace!

30
00:03:21.850 --> 00:03:25.520
Wh-Wh-What's that?
There's a weird smell in the air!

31
00:03:25.520 --> 00:03:29.480
Oh! Found it! A food place!

32
00:03:34.150 --> 00:03:37.200
So? What do you want from me?

33
00:03:37.820 --> 00:03:39.700
To let me capture you quietly.

34
00:03:40.070 --> 00:03:42.660
Sorry. No can do.

35
00:03:43.240 --> 00:03:45.870
Yeah, I figured.

36
00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:52.090
I'm in the middle
of locating another pirate.

37
00:03:52.090 --> 00:03:55.380
Cards on the table,
I'm not here for your head.

38
00:03:55.380 --> 00:03:57.340
So look the other way.

39
00:03:57.340 --> 00:03:59.340
No can do.

40
00:03:59.930 --> 00:04:01.600
See, I'm a Marine...

41
00:04:02.140 --> 00:04:04.430
and you're a pirate.

42
00:04:05.390 --> 00:04:07.890
What a silly reason.

43
00:04:09.190 --> 00:04:10.770
Let's have some fun then.

44
00:04:15.650 --> 00:04:18.240
Gum-Gum...

45
00:04:18.700 --> 00:04:20.450
Rocket!

46
00:04:34.840 --> 00:04:37.300
A food place! I finally found one!

47
00:04:37.880 --> 00:04:40.470
Time to eat! I'm starving!

48
00:04:40.470 --> 00:04:43.260
Old guy! Food! Food! Food!
On the double!

49
00:04:45.930 --> 00:04:49.890
Hurry! Hurry! Hurry!
Food! Food! Food!

50
00:04:49.890 --> 00:04:51.310
Wow!

51
00:04:51.310 --> 00:04:53.360
These are beautiful!

52
00:04:51.350 --> 00:04:56.280
<b>On the Outskirts
of Nanohana</b>

53
00:04:54.320 --> 00:04:56.190
I love these kinds of clothes!

54
00:04:56.190 --> 00:04:59.530
While I realize I asked you
to shop for us, Sanji,

55
00:04:59.530 --> 00:05:02.280
aren't these outfits for dancer girls?

56
00:05:02.280 --> 00:05:05.160
And they look amazing on you!

57
00:05:05.160 --> 00:05:07.080
I asked for ordinary civilian clothes...

58
00:05:07.080 --> 00:05:08.790
Dancers are civilians too!

59
00:05:08.790 --> 00:05:11.000
But we have to cross a desert...

60
00:05:09.660 --> 00:05:11.000
Don't worry!

61
00:05:11.000 --> 00:05:14.210
If you get tired, I'll carry you!

62
00:05:14.920 --> 00:05:16.170
Truly a lost cause.

63
00:05:16.670 --> 00:05:21.970
But, compared to them, you guys
look like a couple of bandits.

64
00:05:21.970 --> 00:05:23.720
What, and you don't?

65
00:05:23.720 --> 00:05:24.640
Chopper!

66
00:05:24.640 --> 00:05:26.260
What are you doing?

67
00:05:27.140 --> 00:05:28.180
It reeks.

68
00:05:28.180 --> 00:05:29.890
That reminds me, where did you go?

69
00:05:29.890 --> 00:05:30.730
Various places!

70
00:05:30.730 --> 00:05:31.980
Is he feeling ill?

71
00:05:31.980 --> 00:05:35.110
Oh, the perfume's getting to him.

72
00:05:35.610 --> 00:05:36.360
Perfume?

73
00:05:36.360 --> 00:05:39.780
Oh, right! Tony has a sensitive nose!

74
00:05:40.400 --> 00:05:41.070
Oh, this...

75
00:05:41.070 --> 00:05:42.910
They are often very potent.

76
00:05:42.910 --> 00:05:44.070
Like this?

77
00:05:44.070 --> 00:05:45.450
Hey! Stop!

78
00:05:45.450 --> 00:05:47.790
My love greatly deepens, Mellorine!

79
00:05:47.790 --> 00:05:49.790
You always this idiotic?

80
00:05:48.830 --> 00:05:49.790
Huh?!

81
00:05:49.790 --> 00:05:54.710
In any case, we've accomplished
our first goal of gathering supplies!

82
00:05:54.710 --> 00:05:55.710
Yes...

83
00:05:55.710 --> 00:05:58.960
We're going to a place
called Yuba, was it?

84
00:05:58.960 --> 00:06:03.380
That's right, but going there
means crossing the desert.

85
00:06:03.380 --> 00:06:07.810
So good! The food here is tasty!

86
00:06:07.810 --> 00:06:12.230
Y-Yeah. Thanks. But...

87
00:06:13.900 --> 00:06:17.690
Well, you... ought to
scram while you can.

88
00:06:17.690 --> 00:06:18.730
How come?

89
00:06:20.280 --> 00:06:22.400
Why, you...!

90
00:06:23.150 --> 00:06:25.110
Who the hell did this?!

91
00:06:27.620 --> 00:06:29.120
What the hell?!

92
00:06:30.080 --> 00:06:33.040
What's the big idea?!

93
00:06:37.210 --> 00:06:40.250
Oh! Apologies
for disturbing your meal!

94
00:06:46.720 --> 00:06:49.680
What idiot would do
something this crazy?!

95
00:06:57.020 --> 00:06:58.190
Lu...!

96
00:06:58.190 --> 00:06:59.020
Hey! Luf–

97
00:06:59.940 --> 00:07:02.650
Straw Hat!

98
00:07:10.280 --> 00:07:13.160
I've been looking for you, Straw Hat!

99
00:07:13.160 --> 00:07:16.540
So you actually came to Alabasta!

100
00:07:22.130 --> 00:07:23.340
Stop eating!

101
00:07:29.470 --> 00:07:31.260
Isn't he...?

102
00:07:33.600 --> 00:07:37.980
I'm Marine Captain Smoker.
I'm in charge of Loguetown.

103
00:07:42.940 --> 00:07:45.780
You're that smoke guy!
What are you doing here?!

104
00:07:45.780 --> 00:07:46.990
Why you...!

105
00:07:47.360 --> 00:07:48.070
Hold it!

106
00:07:50.410 --> 00:07:52.080
Thanks for the meal!

107
00:07:52.410 --> 00:07:53.040
Huh?

108
00:07:55.120 --> 00:07:56.040
Hold it!

109
00:07:57.830 --> 00:08:00.170
Wait, Luffy! It's me!

110
00:08:00.170 --> 00:08:04.670
Hey! Wait up! Hey! Luffy!

111
00:08:06.720 --> 00:08:08.130
They didn't pay...

112
00:08:08.130 --> 00:08:12.300
This is bad! My Gum-Gum moves
don't work on that guy at all!

113
00:08:12.300 --> 00:08:14.140
Gotta just run for now!

114
00:08:14.140 --> 00:08:15.180
Tashigi!

115
00:08:15.180 --> 00:08:18.520
Y-Yes, Captain Smoker?!
Do you need a towel?

116
00:08:18.520 --> 00:08:20.150
This place sure is hot!

117
00:08:20.150 --> 00:08:22.310
Get him! It's Straw Hat!

118
00:08:22.310 --> 00:08:23.230
S-Straw Hat?!

119
00:08:23.940 --> 00:08:25.150
I'll stop him!

120
00:08:31.200 --> 00:08:33.830
Tashigi! Round up the Marines!

121
00:08:33.830 --> 00:08:36.660
Search every nook and cranny
for Straw Hat's crew!

122
00:08:37.080 --> 00:08:38.370
Yes, sir!

123
00:08:38.370 --> 00:08:40.370
People with powers are fighting!

124
00:08:40.370 --> 00:08:41.040
Whoa!

125
00:08:41.960 --> 00:08:44.250
Straw Hat's crew! That means...

126
00:08:48.300 --> 00:08:51.220
Roronoa Zoro is in this city!

127
00:08:53.550 --> 00:08:55.060
White Snake!

128
00:08:59.730 --> 00:09:02.940
Where could Luffy have gone?

129
00:09:02.940 --> 00:09:07.230
Honestly! It's as if our
captain needs a babysitter!

130
00:09:07.230 --> 00:09:08.400
Oh! Nami!

131
00:09:08.820 --> 00:09:10.650
Hey, now! This is bad!

132
00:09:10.650 --> 00:09:13.410
Big trouble's brewing
if we don't make tracks soon.

133
00:09:13.410 --> 00:09:14.620
Big trouble?

134
00:09:14.990 --> 00:09:16.120
The Marines are here.

135
00:09:16.120 --> 00:09:17.120
The Marines?!

136
00:09:17.120 --> 00:09:20.750
The sooner we find Luffy,
the sooner we leave town!

137
00:09:20.750 --> 00:09:21.580
Hey! Hide!

138
00:09:21.580 --> 00:09:22.420
What for?!

139
00:09:22.420 --> 00:09:23.380
What is it?!

140
00:09:26.550 --> 00:09:27.760
The Marines!

141
00:09:27.760 --> 00:09:29.670
There seems to be a big commotion!

142
00:09:29.670 --> 00:09:32.640
Don't let him escape! After him!

143
00:09:32.640 --> 00:09:37.310
Some idiot pirate must be
running around town or something.

144
00:09:38.470 --> 00:09:41.810
Get back here, Straw Hat!

145
00:09:41.810 --> 00:09:42.850
– It was you?!
– It was you?!

146
00:09:44.520 --> 00:09:45.730
Hey, Zoro!

147
00:09:47.730 --> 00:09:49.650
Oh?! So that's where everyone is?!

148
00:09:49.650 --> 00:09:52.030
You idiot! Ditch those guys first!

149
00:09:52.030 --> 00:09:54.740
It's the Straw Hat crew! Over there!

150
00:09:54.740 --> 00:09:57.160
Okay, so... what now?

151
00:09:57.160 --> 00:09:59.200
– We run, obviously!
– Hurry! To the ship!

152
00:09:59.200 --> 00:10:01.290
What are you doing?! Let's get back!

153
00:10:01.290 --> 00:10:02.160
Hey, you!

154
00:10:02.670 --> 00:10:04.500
Stop! Don't let them escape!

155
00:10:04.500 --> 00:10:06.000
Fall back!

156
00:10:06.000 --> 00:10:06.880
Captain!

157
00:10:07.290 --> 00:10:08.840
Straw Hat is mine!

158
00:10:08.840 --> 00:10:11.420
Wh-Whoa! Here he comes!

159
00:10:11.420 --> 00:10:12.800
White Blow!

160
00:10:14.680 --> 00:10:15.720
You're mine!

161
00:10:18.260 --> 00:10:19.270
Heat Haze!

162
00:10:30.730 --> 00:10:31.740
You, huh?

163
00:10:33.070 --> 00:10:34.200
Give it up.

164
00:10:37.700 --> 00:10:39.580
You may be smoke,

165
00:10:39.580 --> 00:10:41.330
but I'm fire.

166
00:10:41.330 --> 00:10:44.710
We're too evenly matched
to settle things between us.

167
00:10:45.170 --> 00:10:47.880
He has devil fruit powers?!

168
00:10:47.880 --> 00:10:49.460
Who is he, anyway?!

169
00:10:49.960 --> 00:10:50.920
Ace?!

170
00:10:51.960 --> 00:10:53.920
You haven't changed a bit, Luffy.

171
00:10:54.260 --> 00:10:58.390
Ace?! Is that you, Ace?!
You ate a devil fruit?!

172
00:10:58.390 --> 00:11:00.390
Yep! The Flame-Flame Fruit!

173
00:11:00.720 --> 00:11:02.850
Captain Smoker!
Securing the perimeter!

174
00:11:03.640 --> 00:11:07.350
No time to chat!
Get moving! I'll catch up!

175
00:11:07.350 --> 00:11:08.860
Leave them to me!

176
00:11:09.270 --> 00:11:10.820
– Go!
– Let's go!

177
00:11:10.820 --> 00:11:11.780
Y-Yeah!

178
00:11:12.610 --> 00:11:13.820
But, Luffy!

179
00:11:13.820 --> 00:11:15.780
Who is that guy?!

180
00:11:33.130 --> 00:11:34.220
White...

181
00:11:34.510 --> 00:11:35.800
Spark!

182
00:11:42.430 --> 00:11:44.100
Wh-What is that?!

183
00:11:44.100 --> 00:11:45.140
A house fire?

184
00:11:45.140 --> 00:11:47.480
No, that's no ordinary fire!

185
00:11:48.730 --> 00:11:50.560
What in the world is happening?

186
00:11:50.560 --> 00:11:52.900
It's a fight between
flame and smoke?!

187
00:11:52.900 --> 00:11:56.360
He did say he ate
the Flame-Flame Fruit.

188
00:11:57.860 --> 00:12:02.030
But, Luffy! Is that guy really
your older brother?

189
00:12:02.030 --> 00:12:04.200
Yup! His name's Ace!

190
00:12:04.750 --> 00:12:07.580
That you have a brother
isn't what's surprising.

191
00:12:07.580 --> 00:12:09.330
Why would he be in the Grand Line?

192
00:12:09.830 --> 00:12:11.340
Ace is a pirate.

193
00:12:11.340 --> 00:12:15.210
He left our island three years
before me to look for the One Piece.

194
00:12:15.210 --> 00:12:16.670
– What?!
– What?!

195
00:12:20.930 --> 00:12:23.680
A-Anyway, let's hurry
back to the ship!

196
00:12:23.680 --> 00:12:25.390
Run before they catch up!

197
00:12:25.390 --> 00:12:26.980
Yes, Nami!

198
00:12:31.980 --> 00:12:36.110
Still, I never thought
I'd see Ace in a place like this!

199
00:12:39.240 --> 00:12:40.990
The path splits here!

200
00:12:40.990 --> 00:12:42.870
Go left, Usopp! Everyone catch that?!

201
00:12:42.870 --> 00:12:45.330
Yes! I'll follow Nami
wherever she goes!

202
00:12:45.330 --> 00:12:47.200
Enough, pervy cook!

203
00:12:47.200 --> 00:12:51.210
So cool! The fireball's
even higher now!

204
00:12:52.380 --> 00:12:55.880
A battle of flame and smoke
really is endless.

205
00:12:57.090 --> 00:12:58.920
But we already knew that.

206
00:13:00.430 --> 00:13:02.550
Where did the Straw Hats go?

207
00:13:02.550 --> 00:13:03.680
They're gone!

208
00:13:03.680 --> 00:13:05.890
So is Ace! We've lost sight of him!

209
00:13:06.390 --> 00:13:10.140
I finally caught up to Straw Hat
in the Grand Line,

210
00:13:10.140 --> 00:13:14.980
but Portgas D. Ace
just had to get in the way.

211
00:13:15.980 --> 00:13:18.900
Hurry and load the supplies!
We're leaving right away!

212
00:13:18.900 --> 00:13:19.950
Hurry!

213
00:13:21.030 --> 00:13:21.990
Unfurl the sails!

214
00:13:24.490 --> 00:13:29.250
Say... We just got to the island,
but are we already leaving?

215
00:13:29.250 --> 00:13:34.040
Yes. This town was only a stopover
for some needed supplies.

216
00:13:34.040 --> 00:13:37.760
Next, we sail the ship up the river
farther into Alabasta.

217
00:13:38.710 --> 00:13:42.050
Our next destination is Erumalu,
the City of Green.

218
00:13:42.050 --> 00:13:43.180
Erumalu?

219
00:13:43.180 --> 00:13:44.350
Hurry!

220
00:13:44.850 --> 00:13:45.850
Pick up the pace!

221
00:13:45.850 --> 00:13:46.890
All set!

222
00:13:46.890 --> 00:13:48.430
Okay! Let's set sail!

223
00:13:51.770 --> 00:13:52.900
Huh?

224
00:13:53.400 --> 00:13:54.690
Y'know...

225
00:13:55.060 --> 00:13:57.900
I get the feeling
we're missing someone...

226
00:13:58.480 --> 00:13:59.780
Huh?!

227
00:14:01.150 --> 00:14:03.490
That's weird.

228
00:14:06.990 --> 00:14:09.290
Where did they go?

229
00:14:09.910 --> 00:14:14.170
Man! I guess my letting you escape
was pretty much pointless.

230
00:14:14.830 --> 00:14:15.540
Hey!

231
00:14:16.090 --> 00:14:17.040
Ace!

232
00:14:19.000 --> 00:14:20.710
Been a while, Luffy.

233
00:14:21.170 --> 00:14:22.510
Right back at you, Ace!

234
00:14:27.260 --> 00:14:28.810
How many years has it been?

235
00:14:29.180 --> 00:14:30.180
Good question.

236
00:14:30.180 --> 00:14:32.810
But Luffy, I see you still
do things at your own pace,

237
00:14:32.810 --> 00:14:34.770
just like when we were kids.

238
00:14:35.350 --> 00:14:36.610
You too, Ace!

239
00:14:36.610 --> 00:14:40.280
I'm surprised you ate a devil fruit,
but besides that, you're the same!

240
00:14:40.280 --> 00:14:43.490
Like when you'd sneak into
the fields, eat 100 watermelons,

241
00:14:43.490 --> 00:14:46.280
and then spit the seeds out
like a gun and run!

242
00:14:46.280 --> 00:14:48.740
That wasn't me! That was you!

243
00:14:48.740 --> 00:14:51.580
Yeah, and they
whupped you good for it!

244
00:14:51.580 --> 00:14:54.750
Again, that was you!
I only watched and laughed!

245
00:15:02.460 --> 00:15:04.220
So we didn't change!

246
00:15:04.220 --> 00:15:05.260
Nope!

247
00:15:06.260 --> 00:15:08.180
Brings back memories!

248
00:15:08.180 --> 00:15:09.140
So...

249
00:15:09.600 --> 00:15:11.720
weren't your friends
looking for you?

250
00:15:11.720 --> 00:15:12.980
Yeah.

251
00:15:12.980 --> 00:15:15.230
But, Ace. What are you
doing in this country?

252
00:15:15.230 --> 00:15:15.940
Huh?

253
00:15:15.940 --> 00:15:19.940
You mean, you didn't get
the message I left back in Drum?

254
00:15:20.270 --> 00:15:21.190
Drum?

255
00:15:21.940 --> 00:15:26.320
Yeah. Don't sweat it,
though. No biggie.

256
00:15:26.320 --> 00:15:29.830
I'm in these waters seeing
to a minor business matter,

257
00:15:29.830 --> 00:15:32.200
so I thought I might look you up.

258
00:15:32.200 --> 00:15:33.160
Minor business?

259
00:15:35.660 --> 00:15:37.620
I joined up with
the Whitebeard Pirates.

260
00:15:38.920 --> 00:15:40.670
Whitebeard Pirates?

261
00:15:41.090 --> 00:15:43.550
Here's the mark
of a Whitebeard Pirate.

262
00:15:43.550 --> 00:15:44.720
It's my pride.

263
00:15:44.720 --> 00:15:45.380
Oh?

264
00:15:47.630 --> 00:15:50.800
So, Luffy, how 'bout joining
Whitebeard's crew?

265
00:15:50.800 --> 00:15:52.470
Your friends can come too.

266
00:15:53.560 --> 00:15:54.520
No.

267
00:15:57.480 --> 00:15:59.060
Oh well, just thought I'd ask.

268
00:15:59.560 --> 00:16:03.440
Whitebeard is the greatest pirate
I've ever known.

269
00:16:04.940 --> 00:16:08.990
I'm gonna help him
become King of the Pirates...

270
00:16:09.110 --> 00:16:11.280
It won't be you, Luffy.

271
00:16:11.280 --> 00:16:13.910
That's fine! Then I guess
we gotta fight!

272
00:16:16.540 --> 00:16:19.000
I'm gonna be King of the Pirates.

273
00:16:20.460 --> 00:16:23.300
Hey! Don't drink it all, Luffy!

274
00:16:30.930 --> 00:16:33.470
Something big happening in town?

275
00:16:33.470 --> 00:16:37.770
Smoker and all his men
left the ship.

276
00:16:38.390 --> 00:16:41.270
But... this is perfect!

277
00:16:41.270 --> 00:16:43.230
Here's my chance to try and escape!

278
00:16:44.360 --> 00:16:46.570
Mr. 11.

279
00:16:46.570 --> 00:16:54.700
<b>Full
Fledged</b>

280
00:16:47.530 --> 00:16:51.700
You know my codename, so you
must be members of Baroque Works!

281
00:16:51.700 --> 00:16:52.820
Millions, I take it?

282
00:16:52.820 --> 00:16:54.990
Hurry and untie me!

283
00:16:54.700 --> 00:17:01.830
<b>Full
Fledged</b>

284
00:16:54.990 --> 00:16:57.830
Indeed, we are members
of Baroque Works.

285
00:16:57.830 --> 00:17:01.830
We're billions, though.
We're next to become number agents.

286
00:17:01.830 --> 00:17:09.800
<b>Full
Fledged</b>

287
00:17:01.830 --> 00:17:08.300
Mr. 11, you're barely an agent, seeing
as you're not much stronger than us.

288
00:17:08.300 --> 00:17:10.550
O-Oh! I see!

289
00:17:10.550 --> 00:17:14.760
My mistake, billions.
But could you hurry and untie me?

290
00:17:15.760 --> 00:17:17.520
That'd be stupid of us!

291
00:17:17.430 --> 00:17:18.060
<b>Full
Fledged</b>

292
00:17:19.140 --> 00:17:25.570
<b>Full
Fledged</b>

293
00:17:19.140 --> 00:17:25.400
With you gone, one of us will get
promoted to a number agent.

294
00:17:27.230 --> 00:17:30.030
So let's empty
one of the agents' seats!

295
00:17:30.360 --> 00:17:32.490
W-Wait!

296
00:17:38.950 --> 00:17:40.830
Hey!

297
00:17:43.290 --> 00:17:45.460
Fire Fist Ace is in this town!

298
00:17:45.460 --> 00:17:46.170
What?!

299
00:17:46.170 --> 00:17:50.970
<b>Full
Fledged</b>

300
00:17:46.800 --> 00:17:48.130
Fire Fist Ace?!

301
00:17:48.130 --> 00:17:50.970
The Second Division commander
of the Whitebeard Pirates?

302
00:17:51.590 --> 00:17:56.220
If we can take down Ace,
we're guaranteed to be number agents!

303
00:18:01.020 --> 00:18:04.810
Sh-Should we really be
setting sail without Luffy?

304
00:18:05.310 --> 00:18:08.070
The Marines will be
all over the harbors.

305
00:18:08.070 --> 00:18:10.440
We need to hide the ship first.

306
00:18:10.440 --> 00:18:13.030
There should be
a hidden cove up ahead!

307
00:18:13.530 --> 00:18:16.990
And we look for Luffy
when the coast is clear.

308
00:18:17.370 --> 00:18:20.950
Man... If it's not one thing
with Luffy, it's another!

309
00:18:23.330 --> 00:18:25.920
Our captain... Reliable as ever...

310
00:18:28.840 --> 00:18:29.840
Oh! The ocean!

311
00:18:29.840 --> 00:18:31.800
See your ship?

312
00:18:33.180 --> 00:18:34.970
End of the line!

313
00:18:35.430 --> 00:18:36.510
Oh!

314
00:18:36.510 --> 00:18:37.890
There it is!

315
00:18:39.350 --> 00:18:42.980
Hey! Over here! Guys!

316
00:18:42.980 --> 00:18:44.810
Hey, Luffy. Go on ahe–

317
00:18:44.810 --> 00:18:46.230
Never mind.

318
00:18:48.440 --> 00:18:50.530
Oh! There he is! It's Luffy!

319
00:18:50.530 --> 00:18:51.860
I found Luffy!

320
00:18:51.860 --> 00:18:52.820
Where is he?

321
00:18:52.820 --> 00:18:55.570
Yeah. That's definitely his dumb mug.

322
00:18:55.570 --> 00:18:56.280
Huh?!

323
00:19:00.700 --> 00:19:02.580
I'm back!

324
00:19:03.540 --> 00:19:06.290
Sanji! Tony!

325
00:19:07.540 --> 00:19:09.170
Oh, come on!

326
00:19:09.540 --> 00:19:10.800
Not again.

327
00:19:12.670 --> 00:19:14.800
Sorry about that, Sanji and Chopper.

328
00:19:14.800 --> 00:19:18.220
How do you never learn
from any of this?!

329
00:19:18.220 --> 00:19:19.890
I oughta just gut you here!

330
00:19:19.890 --> 00:19:22.680
Yeah! Do you even realize
the trouble you've caused?!

331
00:19:22.680 --> 00:19:25.020
Try to act somewhat like a captain!

332
00:19:25.850 --> 00:19:26.900
Sorry.

333
00:19:26.900 --> 00:19:28.520
Oh, that's right! Ace!

334
00:19:29.150 --> 00:19:29.940
Ace?

335
00:19:29.940 --> 00:19:31.480
Your brother was with you?

336
00:19:31.900 --> 00:19:34.650
Is it okay to just leave him there?

337
00:19:35.400 --> 00:19:38.240
Oh, it's okay! Ace is pretty strong!

338
00:19:38.240 --> 00:19:40.030
He's strong?

339
00:19:40.410 --> 00:19:44.120
Yup. Back in the day he hadn't
eaten the Flame-Flame Fruit,

340
00:19:44.120 --> 00:19:47.500
but I still never beat him
in a single fight!

341
00:19:47.960 --> 00:19:50.130
Ace is that strong!

342
00:19:50.130 --> 00:19:53.000
There's a flesh-and-blood person
you could never beat?!

343
00:19:53.000 --> 00:19:55.470
So the monster's big bro
is an even bigger monster.

344
00:19:55.470 --> 00:19:58.840
That's right! I lost to him all the time!

345
00:19:59.720 --> 00:20:02.390
But now, I'd beat him good!

346
00:20:02.390 --> 00:20:05.180
Guessing you've got
nothing to base that on.

347
00:20:07.020 --> 00:20:08.350
Who...

348
00:20:10.310 --> 00:20:11.520
can beat who now?!

349
00:20:13.360 --> 00:20:16.320
Oh! Ace! These are
the friends we talked about!

350
00:20:16.700 --> 00:20:20.570
Oh! Thank you all for looking
after my kid brother.

351
00:20:20.570 --> 00:20:22.160
– Huh? Oh, not at all.
– Huh? Oh, not at all.

352
00:20:22.910 --> 00:20:27.620
And maybe he's sometimes
a bit too much to handle, but...

353
00:20:28.120 --> 00:20:29.460
– No, not at all.
– No, not at all.

354
00:20:29.460 --> 00:20:31.380
Take good care of him.

355
00:20:32.130 --> 00:20:34.500
Well, you two
probably want to catch up.

356
00:20:34.500 --> 00:20:36.840
Come on in.
I'll make some tea.

357
00:20:36.840 --> 00:20:39.890
No, that's okay. Don't trouble
yourself on my account.

358
00:20:44.640 --> 00:20:46.640
T-Talk about unexpected...

359
00:20:46.640 --> 00:20:48.100
That's for sure.

360
00:20:48.100 --> 00:20:51.730
I'd have thought he'd be
as reckless as Luffy.

361
00:20:51.730 --> 00:20:55.980
There's no way this
sensible man is Luffy's brother!

362
00:20:55.980 --> 00:20:58.240
He's nice and he cares
about his kid brother.

363
00:20:58.240 --> 00:21:00.360
Brothers can be so wonderful!

364
00:21:00.360 --> 00:21:03.240
The sea is just full of surprises.

365
00:21:03.240 --> 00:21:05.240
Come now, everyone!

366
00:21:05.240 --> 00:21:08.250
See! Aren't these guys neat?!

367
00:21:11.960 --> 00:21:14.540
Baroque Works!
Those are the billions' ships!

368
00:21:14.540 --> 00:21:19.510
Fire Fist Ace and Straw Hat Luffy!
Don't think you've gotten away!

369
00:21:19.510 --> 00:21:23.180
We'll show you just what
Baroque Works' billions are made of!

370
00:21:23.680 --> 00:21:25.310
Those guys again?

371
00:21:25.310 --> 00:21:28.140
Luffy. I'll take out the trash.

372
00:21:30.690 --> 00:21:32.350
What's he going to do?

373
00:21:32.350 --> 00:21:34.190
Especially in that little boat...

374
00:21:36.320 --> 00:21:41.660
Let's see the Whitebeard Pirates'
Second Division commander in action.

375
00:21:42.410 --> 00:21:45.780
Here he comes! Fire Fist Ace!

376
00:21:45.780 --> 00:21:49.330
Just try us, hotshot,
but it's you against five ships!

377
00:21:52.540 --> 00:21:53.210
He jumped!

378
00:21:53.830 --> 00:21:55.340
F-Fire!

379
00:21:55.340 --> 00:21:57.800
Blast him into a watery grave!

380
00:22:07.010 --> 00:22:08.010
Fire Fist!

381
00:22:32.210 --> 00:22:34.210
A-Amazing!

382
00:22:45.930 --> 00:22:47.220
Captain Smoker!

383
00:22:48.100 --> 00:22:52.600
Straw Hat Luffy and his crew
are nowhere to be found.

384
00:22:52.600 --> 00:22:54.690
What do you make of this, Tashigi?

385
00:22:55.440 --> 00:22:57.690
Vivi was with them.

386
00:22:57.690 --> 00:23:02.490
Vivi? Princess Nefertari Vivi
was with the Straw Hats?

387
00:23:02.940 --> 00:23:04.450
She must be a hostage.

388
00:23:04.450 --> 00:23:08.120
The princess' abduction
must be part of some plot.

389
00:23:08.620 --> 00:23:12.450
No. Vivi was acting like
she was part of their crew.

390
00:23:12.950 --> 00:23:16.420
The princess? Part of their crew?

391
00:23:17.040 --> 00:23:20.550
There's something
afoot in this country.

392
00:23:20.960 --> 00:23:22.920
Captain Smoker!

393
00:23:22.920 --> 00:23:24.260
I'm sorry, sir!

394
00:23:24.260 --> 00:23:28.680
Mr. 11 was done in by someone
while tied up on the ship!

395
00:23:28.680 --> 00:23:31.260
We still haven't located
the Straw Hats, either!

396
00:23:31.260 --> 00:23:35.350
Get it together. I believe
I know where they're headed.

397
00:23:35.850 --> 00:23:38.020
He's gunning for Crocodile.

398
00:23:38.270 --> 00:23:39.860
Crocodile?!

399
00:23:39.860 --> 00:23:41.980
A pirate backed by the government,

400
00:23:42.480 --> 00:23:44.440
one of the Seven Warlords of the Sea?!

401
00:23:44.440 --> 00:23:47.660
You know I hate
the Seven Warlords, right?

402
00:23:47.660 --> 00:23:49.620
Especially that detestable man.

403
00:23:49.620 --> 00:23:53.950
B-But he's currently an ally
to the Marines and the government!

404
00:23:54.580 --> 00:23:57.960
He's always been clever, that pirate.

405
00:23:57.960 --> 00:24:01.710
He's not the type to roll over
and beg for the government. Not him!

406
00:24:02.340 --> 00:24:04.880
Tashigi! Remember this one thing!

407
00:24:04.880 --> 00:24:06.720
A pirate's a pirate,

408
00:24:06.720 --> 00:24:08.260
no matter his status!

409
00:24:10.050 --> 00:24:14.180
If we head toward Crocodile,
we'll find Straw Hat.

410
00:24:14.180 --> 00:24:17.060
It'll all come to light
when we get there.

411
00:24:17.060 --> 00:24:20.310
And next time, you won't
get away, Straw Hat!

412
00:24:21.270 --> 00:24:24.530
Ace is one of us now!

413
00:24:24.530 --> 00:24:25.740
– Cheers!
– Cheers!

414
00:24:25.740 --> 00:24:28.410
Whad'ya mean, I'm one of you?

415
00:24:30.620 --> 00:24:32.080
Here's to delicious drinks!

416
00:24:32.080 --> 00:24:33.950
– Cheers!
– Cheers!

417
00:24:32.830 --> 00:24:34.580
Pay it no mind!

418
00:24:33.950 --> 00:24:35.660
Here's to delicious drinks!

419
00:24:34.580 --> 00:24:38.580
They'll find any excuse
to have a drink!

420
00:24:35.660 --> 00:24:36.910
– Cheers!
– Cheers!

421
00:24:36.910 --> 00:24:38.580
Here's to delicious drinks!

422
00:24:38.580 --> 00:24:41.000
– Medicine is gross!
– Medicine is gross!

423
00:24:43.840 --> 00:24:46.840
Ace! Are you sure you won't join us?

424
00:24:47.720 --> 00:24:50.090
I'm chasing a certain man.

425
00:24:51.850 --> 00:24:53.300
His name's Blackbeard.

426
00:24:53.680 --> 00:24:55.020
Blackbeard?

427
00:24:55.020 --> 00:24:57.270
He's the pirate who attacked
the Kingdom of Drum!

428
00:24:58.640 --> 00:25:01.900
He once belonged
to Whitebeard's Second Division,

429
00:25:01.900 --> 00:25:03.730
one of my own men.

430
00:25:03.730 --> 00:25:06.650
But he committed the most
grievous act any pirate could.

431
00:25:06.650 --> 00:25:08.990
He killed a crewmate
and jumped ship.

432
00:25:09.780 --> 00:25:13.830
Since I'm the commander,
I gotta take responsibility for him.

433
00:25:13.830 --> 00:25:16.620
So that's why you're
chasing after him?

434
00:25:17.370 --> 00:25:20.040
We've just started up
the Sandora River.

435
00:25:20.040 --> 00:25:22.380
First, we'll land at Erumalu.

436
00:25:22.380 --> 00:25:25.420
We'll then head into Alabasta's
interior to reach Yuba here!

437
00:25:26.250 --> 00:25:28.920
That's where we'll find
the leader of the Rebellion.

438
00:25:28.920 --> 00:25:31.380
I see. Yuba it is then.

439
00:25:31.380 --> 00:25:34.760
I'll follow Nami and Vivi
wherever they go!

440
00:25:34.760 --> 00:25:36.350
Drop dead, Love Cook.

441
00:25:36.350 --> 00:25:37.970
Say what?! You–

442
00:25:37.970 --> 00:25:41.100
A-Anyways! It seems we'll be
traveling together for a bit!

443
00:25:41.100 --> 00:25:44.310
Yeah, yeah! His brother is
more than welcome here!

444
00:25:46.190 --> 00:25:47.900
Let's have some fun, Ace!

445
00:25:48.650 --> 00:25:51.490
– Yeah!
– Yeah!
